hist":31.2,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.01975222281004202,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.44703825473817477,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":25.5,"_gate_incr_roic":0.04212705795335511,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":30.7,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.2433883941985778,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.01606097562892317,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":46.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06426087489730392,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":57.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.048028284346881556,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":49.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.033898971599928746,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":48.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.019063396038557334,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":26.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011421646240153249,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":81.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.010980001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Federal Realty Investment Trust is a recognized leader in the ownership, operation and redevelopment of high-quality retail-based properties located primarily in major coastal markets and select underserved regions with strong economic and demographic fundamentals. Federal Realty's mission is to deliver long-term, sustainable growth through investing in communities where retail demand exceeds supply. This includes a portfolio of open-air shopping centers and mixed-use destinations\u0097such as Santana Row, Pike & Rose, and Assembly Row, which together reflect the company's ability to create distinctive, high-performing environments that serve as vibrant destinations for their communities. Federal Realty's 103 properties include approximately 3,700 tenants in 28.8 million commercial square feet, and approximately 2,700 residential units. Federal Realty has increased its quarterly dividends to its shareholders for 59 consecutive years, the longest record in the REIT industry. Federal Realty Investment Trust is based in North Bethesda, Maryland. Federal Realty Investment Trust was incorporated in 1962 in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Donald C. Wood CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 314 people. Revenue per employee of $4.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $47K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Federal Realty Investment Trust is a mid-cap real estate business with a $9.7B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 122% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.222137252478422},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Payout ratio of 91% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 24% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Federal Realty Investment Trust (NYSE:FRT) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $1.11 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonl